{"nodes": [{"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_overview", "label": "Connecting Postgres (and Other Adapters) Guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documents the ports-and-adapters (hexagonal) design of the booking system: every external dependency sits behind an interface, and swapping an adapter means writing one class and changing one line in container.ts."}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_bookingrepository", "label": "BookingRepository (port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Interface hiding the concrete storage adapter from use cases/Server Actions/components. Postgres implementation must guarantee createIfSlotFree/rescheduleIfSlotFree atomicity, unlike the single-threaded in-memory dev adapter."}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_notificationservice", "label": "NotificationService (port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_servicerepository", "label": "ServiceRepository (port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_solicitorrepository", "label": "SolicitorRepository (port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_officerepository", "label": "OfficeRepository (port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_spamguard", "label": "SpamGuard (port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_ratelimiter", "label": "RateLimiter (port, consume(key, now))", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_calendarsyncservice", "label": "CalendarSyncService (future port)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not built: two-way calendar sync needs a registered OAuth app (Google Calendar API / Microsoft Graph), a client secret and consent screen, and per-client refresh-token storage (which itself requires the Postgres swap first) plus a live public deployment. Additive later: a port alongside the existing ones, called from createBooking/cancelBooking/rescheduleBooking the same way NotificationService is today."}, {"id": "src_application_booking_ports_emailmessage", "label": "EmailMessage (type)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_container", "label": "container.ts (composition root)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single composition root wiring concrete adapters to ports; no use case, Server Action, or component ever imports a concrete adapter directly."}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_inmemorybookingrepository", "label": "InMemoryBookingRepository (dev adapter)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checks-then-inserts synchronously; safe only because JS is single-threaded per request. Not safe for Postgres without a SERIALIZABLE transaction or a DB-level EXCLUDE constraint."}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_staticservicerepository", "label": "StaticServiceRepository (dev adapter)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_staticsolicitorrepository", "label": "StaticSolicitorRepository (dev adapter)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_staticofficerepository", "label": "StaticOfficeRepository (dev adapter)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_consolenotificationservice", "label": "ConsoleNotificationService (dev adapter)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Logs instead of sending; recommended production swap is Resend for first-class Next.js support, simple API, generous free tier."}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_honeypotspamguard", "label": "HoneypotSpamGuard", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_container_inmemoryratelimiter", "label": "InMemoryRateLimiter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only shares state within one Node process; fine for a single long-running server but breaks once deployed across multiple serverless instances, since each instance gets its own memory (the '5 attempts per 15 minutes' limit becomes per-instance). Needs a Redis-backed swap (e.g. Upstash) at scale."}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_booking_postgres_prismabookingrepository_prismabookingrepository", "label": "PrismaBookingRepository (planned)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_infrastructure_booking_notifications_resendnotificationservice_resendnotificationservice", "label": "ResendNotificationService (planned)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_application_booking_emailcomposer_emailcomposer", "label": "emailComposer.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every email's actual content (subject/html/text/attachments) is already fully composed here; a NotificationService adapter only has to transport it."}, {"id": "src_domain_scheduling_ics_ics", "label": "ics.ts (.ics file generation)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_domain_scheduling_calendarlinks_calendarlinks", "label": "calendarLinks.ts (Add to Google/Outlook links)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_postgres_exclude_constraint", "label": "Postgres EXCLUDE Constraint (btree_gist) Design", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recommended over a SERIALIZABLE transaction: an EXCLUDE constraint using btree_gist over (solicitor_slug, tstzrange(slot_start_utc, slot_end_utc)) makes double-booking impossible even under concurrent requests, a guarantee an application-level check alone can't provide. rescheduleIfSlotFree relies on the same constraint by catching the violation error on UPDATE."}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_resend", "label": "Resend (email delivery service)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_upstash", "label": "Upstash + @upstash/ratelimit (Redis-backed limiter)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_vercel_cron", "label": "Vercel Cron (/vercel.json, hourly)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CRON_SECRET set in deployment env vars lets Vercel Cron authenticate automatically; any other scheduler (GitHub Actions cron, traditional crontab with curl -H Authorization Bearer) works identically."}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_createbooking", "label": "createBooking (use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_cancelbooking", "label": "cancelBooking (use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_reschedulebooking", "label": "rescheduleBooking (use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_sendduereminders", "label": "sendDueReminders (use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_createreview", "label": "createReview (future use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Would mirror createBooking's shape and be gated behind the same SpamGuard port the booking form already uses, so no new spam-protection code is needed."}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_listreviews", "label": "listReviews (use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_listvideotestimonials", "label": "listVideoTestimonials (use case)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/prisma/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_prisma_readme_googleplacesreviewrepository", "label": "GooglePlacesReviewRepository (hypothetical future adapter)", "file_type": "concept", "sour